add('line','Follow the line. Inspect the connection.','INSPECT','inspect',
 ['A line joins two points. Follow its path.','Inspect: look carefully at where the line goes.','The arrow guides the eye from the label to its object.'],
 [('spect','look','Latin'),('in-','into, in this word','Latin')],['inspect · look carefully','spectator · someone who watches','inspection · a careful check'],
 'Name the relationship: a line runs along an edge, goes through an area, or connects one thing to another. The root spect is a useful clue in words about looking.',
 ['The line connects A to B.','The line connects the label to the picture, so the relationship is clear.','The line that connects the label to the picture makes the reference explicit.'],
 ['Connect A to B: use to for the destination.','So connects the visible choice to its result.','The clause beginning with that identifies which line you mean.'],
 'Which sentence matches the line that joins the two points?', ['The line connects A to B.','The line connects A at B.','The line connects A under B.'],0,'Connect one thing to another: the line joins A and B.',
 'Before printing, a designer inspects every connector to check that it points to the right object.', ['Looks at each connector carefully.','Deletes every connector.','Changes every connector to red.'],0,'Spect suggests looking; checking where each line points confirms that inspect means examine carefully.',
 'Point to a line in a guide example. Say what it connects, divides, or guides.',[E+'inspect',E+'spectator'])
add('color','One hue. A whole word family.','MONOCHROMATIC','mono',
 ['Many hues compete: red, blue, green, and gold.','Mono means one. The colors move into one hue family.','Different lightness levels; one hue. This palette is monochromatic.'],
 [('mono-','one','Greek'),('chromat-','color','Greek'),('-ic','often makes an adjective: related to','Greek origin'),('multi-','many','Latin')],
 ['monochromatic · one hue family','multicolored · several colors','monolingual / multilingual · one language / several languages'],
 'Use word parts as clues, then check the picture and sentence. Monochromatic does not mean every swatch has identical lightness. Mono and chroma are Greek; multi is Latin.',
 ['This palette uses one hue.','The palette is monochromatic because it uses lighter and darker greens.','Although the values differ, the palette remains monochromatic because the swatches share a hue.'],
 ['A hue is a color family, such as green.','Because gives visible evidence for the design term.','Although signals a difference that does not change the conclusion.'],
 'The green swatches vary from light to dark. Why are they monochromatic?', ['They share one hue family.','They must all have the same lightness.','They use every hue on the wheel.'],0,'Mono points to one; the picture confirms one green hue with different values.',
 'A multilingual notice gives the opening details in English, Bangla, and Arabic. What does multilingual mean here?', ['Using several languages.','Using only one language.','Using no written words.'],0,'Multi means many; the three named languages confirm the meaning. A useful reading habit, including for IELTS: word parts → context → likely meaning.',
 'Choose a palette from the guide. Describe its hue relationship and say what helped you decode the term.',[E+'monochromatic',E+'multi-'])
add('shape','Let the adjective show the shape.','ROUNDED','shape',
 ['Sharp corners: an angular shape.','The corners soften while the word ROUNDED rounds off.','Rounded is an adjective: a rounded shape.'],
 [],['shape → shaped','angle → angular','round → rounded'],
 'An adjective usually comes before the noun it describes: a rounded shape, an angular shape. A/an follows the next sound: a rounded shape; an angular shape.',
 ['It is a rounded shape.','The rounded shape has curved edges, whereas the angular shape has corners.','The angular silhouette creates a different impression from the rounded one; audience context still matters.'],
 ['Say a + adjective + noun.','Whereas connects two visible differences.','Describe the feature before interpreting the impression.'],
 'Which phrase correctly names a shape with sharp corners?', ['An angular shape.','An shape angular.','A angular shape.'],0,'Angular starts with a vowel sound; the adjective comes before shape.',
 'The designer replaces an angular border with a rounded one. What changes?', ['Sharp corners become curved.','A flat image becomes a real object.','The wording disappears.'],0,'Rounded describes the curved outline, not a change to the text or physical dimension.',
 'Compare a geometric and an organic example. Describe the outlines before guessing their effect.')
add('texture','Say what a surface looks like.','WOVEN','texture',
 ['Separate strands cross over and under.','The strands weave together through the letters.','Woven describes the visible result of weaving.'],
 [('tex / text','weave; a historical root family','Latin')],['texture · surface appearance or feel','textile · woven cloth / fabric','text · historically connected to weaving words together'],
 'A screen image can look rough, smooth, or woven. Use looks + adjective for visible evidence. Texture and textile share a Latin weaving history; this is a word family, not a rule for splitting every text- word.',
 ['The surface looks woven.','The texture looks woven because the strands cross over and under.','The image suggests a woven surface; we cannot judge its actual tactile feel from the picture alone.'],
 ['Looks + adjective: looks rough, looks smooth.','Woven is the irregular past participle of weave.','Suggests distinguishes visual appearance from physical evidence.'],
 'You are describing a photo of rough stone. Which sentence keeps the claim visual?', ['The stone looks rough.','I can feel the stone through the screen.','The stone looks roughly.'],0,'Looks takes the adjective rough. The photo shows appearance, not direct tactile experience.',
 'A textile designer repeats interlaced strands in a fabric pattern. Which meaning fits textile?', ['Cloth or fabric.','A type of battery.','An empty margin.'],0,'The weaving root is a clue; interlaced strands and fabric confirm the meaning.',
 'Choose two source textures. Describe how they look, then explain one use for each.',[E+'texture',E+'textile',E+'text'])
