 'Primary can mean main in importance, not only first in time. First, next, and finally organize your explanation of reading order. Check the context: primary colors use the same word differently.',
 ['First, I notice the title.','First, I notice the title. Next, I read the date. Finally, I find the place.','The title has primary emphasis, while the date and location provide secondary and tertiary information.'],
 ['First introduces the first noticed detail.','Reading order should support what the viewer needs.','Importance depends on the brief, not a universal order for all posters.'],
 'The title is largest, the date medium, and the location smallest. Which explains the order?', ['First the title, next the date, finally the location.','Finally the title, first the date, next the location.','Everything has the same visual importance.'],0,'The sizes establish a visible order of emphasis.',
 'The primary objective of the notice is to show where to register. What does primary mean here?', ['Main or most important.','Only red, yellow, and blue.','A small decorative detail.'],0,'Prim supplies a first/main clue; objective makes importance the relevant sense.',
