 'Simplicity in language is editing with a purpose. Keep the audience, action, and essential details. Brevity can help, but deleting the date or place makes an invitation less useful.',
 ['Join us Friday at 4 pm.','Join us Friday at 4 pm at the community hall.','The shorter invitation preserves the action, time, and place while removing redundant wording.'],
 ['Join us is a direct invitation.','Keep the place if the reader needs it.','Concise does not mean incomplete.'],
